---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Pacing is a decision about time" currentPath="/manifesto/foundations/pacing">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Entry</a> / <a href="/manifesto">Manifesto</a> / <a href="/manifesto/foundations">Foundations</a> / Pacing
  </div>

  <article class="principle-document">
    <header class="principle-header">
      <div class="principle-meta">
        <span class="principle-number">I.3</span>
        <span class="plate-id">E01-P04</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Pacing is a decision about time</h1>
      <p class="abstract">Pacing determines how understanding forms by controlling when information is revealed.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="principle-content">
      <h2>Statement</h2>
      <p>Pacing is not a performance choice.</p>
      <p>It is a structural decision about time.</p>

      <h2>Context</h2>
      <p>
        Systems often confuse pacing with urgency—using speed to create pressure. But pacing is about cognitive rhythm: the rate at which information can be absorbed without overwhelming the user's capacity to process it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deliberate deceleration is not inefficiency. It is respect for how understanding actually forms.
      </p>

      <h2>Application</h2>
      <p>
        Pacing manifests through consistent intervals. Content unfolds at a predictable rate—never accelerating to create drama, never stalling to withhold. Each page operates at the same cognitive speed, allowing users to traverse depth rather than breadth.
      </p>

      <h2>Citation</h2>
      <p class="citation-text">
        This principle may be cited as: <strong>I.3 (Pacing)</strong> or by plate reference <strong>E01-P04</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
